{"id": "163008", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=163008", "title": "El Salto", "text": "El Salto is a town of 24,000 people (2015) in the state of Durango, Mexico.\nUnderstand.\nEl Salto is a town and seat of the municipality of Pueblo Nuevo in the southwestern part of the Mexican state of Durango. It is situated on a pine-forested plateau about ft above sea level in the Sierra Madre Mountain range, the town is home to a large lumber industry and a military base. The pine forests around the area provide habitat for a large number of birds, mammals and reptile species.\nClimate.\nThanks to its location in the high plateau of the Sierra Madre Occidental it receives abundant rain during the summer months. The town experiences mild but rainy summers, and relatively dry and chilly winters with freezing night temperatures. Winter months witness the occasional snow shower.\nGet in.\nThe town can be accessed on the Old Mexican Federal Route 40. It is approximately 100 km from the capital of Durango.\nDo.\nEl Salto has places to practice rappelling, mountaineering and zip-lining.\nConnect.\nAs of Dec 2021, El Salto has a basic mobile signal from Telcel but nothing from other carriers. 4G has not reached this area."}
{"id": "163028", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=163028", "title": "Khuzdar District", "text": "Khuzdar is a district in the Balochistan province of Pakistan.\nEat.\nAwaami Restaurant: If you want to eat something to satisfy your appetite, you can visit this beautiful restaurant. It remained open 24 hours a day, so it would prove helpful for you if you visited this beautiful place."}
