{"id": "163580", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=163580", "title": "Tanauan (Batangas)", "text": "Tanauan is a city in Batangas, Philippines\nUnderstand.\nTanauan originated as a fortress built by natives and Augustinian Friars; the name \"Tanauan\" is derived from \"tanaw\" (to look out of a window). It is also historically renowned as the hometown of Apolinario Mabini and other revolutionaries, as well as Jose P. Laurel, who was installed as president of the Philippines during the Japanese occupation in World War II. The town center used to be at the shore of Taal Lake, but was transferred further inland after being devastated over the centuries by multiple eruptions of Taal Volcano.\nThe city has gained national notoriety after the public humiliation campaigns against drug addicts and robbers by mayor Antonio Halili on his first term from 2013 to 2018; he was assassinated in July 2018 by unknown assailants. Chances of being involved in a crime is low, but illegal drugs can be found at rough spots in the city.\nno population data for this page\nGet in.\nMost travelers enter Tanauan through its eponymous exit on the Southern Tagalog Arterial Road (STAR) Tollway. A parallel alternate route is the congested Jose P. Laurel Highway (Route 4) from Santo Tomas.\nGet around.\nTricycles are the main form of public transportation around town.\nStay safe.\nThe most serious nature-related safety issue in Tanauan is the threat of Taal Volcano. The 2020 eruption led to multiple barangays within a 14 to 17-kilometer danger zone radius surrounding the volcano being placed under a \"lockdown\" (evacuated and abandoned) two months before the word became synonymous with the COVID-19 pandemic. While that eruption did not escalate, authorities fear that a full eruption could generate pyroclastic surges that could traverse Taal Lake and obliterate low-lying areas of Tanauan. Hence it is best to regularly check the volcano's alert levels and heed instructions by authorities in cases of heightened activity or a major eruption. \nPHIVOLCS maintains an alert level system of 1 to 5, with 5 being the highest. Avoid all but necessary travel to the area if Level 3 is raised, and do not travel at all to Tanauan once alert level 4 is in place."}
